It wouldn't be Nethack with just 50 rules, and you'd probably want to
write the item/monster database by hand, to get reasonable results.

(Nethack has a lot more than 50 rules. You can limit it to 50 or so and
still get very complex behaviour, but only by combining them; you'd also
need to use floats where Nethack uses booleans. Firebrand wouldn't be a
sword with the "firey" attribute, it would be a sword with the
"temperature in blade" attribute set way above room temperature.)

There would also be quite a bit of stuff under the surface; I/O, AI for
the monsters, sight-line algorithms and so on; the difference is that
changing it would be a lot easier.

